{% doc %}
  Default legal HTML for privacy, terms, and IPR house pages.
  Matches theme/legal/*.md. Merchant richtext in the section overrides this.

  @param {string} document - privacy, terms, or ipr
{% enddoc %}

{%- case document -%}
  {%- when 'privacy' -%}
    <h2>1. Who we are</h2>
    <p>
      This Privacy Policy is <strong>template copy requiring lawyer review</strong>. It is not legal advice.
      For the purposes of this placeholder, the operator of the Maison Tavo storefront is Kartavya
      (together with Maison Tavo, “we”, “us”). Contact:
      {% if shop.email != blank %}
        <a href="mailto:{{ shop.email }}">{{ shop.email }}</a>
      {% else %}
        the email address published on this store
      {% endif %}
      and <a href="https://kartavya.tech" target="_blank" rel="noopener">kartavya.tech</a>.
    </p>
    <h2>2. Scope</h2>
    <p>
      This notice describes how we may collect, use, store, and share personal information when you visit
      {{ shop.name }}, create an account, place an order, contact us, or otherwise interact with our Shopify-hosted
      storefront and related services (including checkout, customer accounts, and email).
    </p>
    <h2>3. Information we collect</h2>
    <p>Depending on how you use the store, we may process:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Identity and contact data (name, email, shipping and billing addresses, phone number).</li>
      <li>Order and transaction data (products purchased, payment status, fulfilment details). Payment card data is processed by Shopify and payment providers; we do not intend to store full card numbers.</li>
      <li>Account data if you register (login identifiers, order history, saved addresses, preferences).</li>
      <li>Technical and usage data (IP address, device and browser type, approximate location, pages viewed, referring URLs) via Shopify, cookies, and similar technologies.</li>
      <li>Communications you send us (enquiries, reviews, returns correspondence).</li>
      <li>Marketing preferences (newsletter signup, consent records where required).</li>
    </ul>
    <h2>4. How we use information</h2>
    <p>We use personal information to:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Provide, fulfil, and administer orders, returns, exchanges, and customer service.</li>
      <li>Operate accounts, authentication, and fraud prevention.</li>
      <li>Comply with tax, accounting, consumer, and other legal obligations.</li>
      <li>Improve the storefront, diagnose issues, and understand aggregated shopping behaviour.</li>
      <li>Send service messages (order updates) and, where permitted, marketing about Maison Tavo.</li>
    </ul>
    <h2>5. Legal bases (placeholder)</h2>
    <p>
      Where data protection laws require a legal basis, we may rely on performance of a contract, legitimate
      interests (for example securing the store and understanding how it is used), compliance with law, and
      consent (for example optional marketing cookies or newsletters). This paragraph must be rewritten for
      the jurisdictions in which Maison Tavo actually sells.
    </p>
    <h2>6. Sharing</h2>
    <p>
      We share information with service providers who assist the house, including Shopify Inc. and its
      affiliates, payment processors, fulfilment and shipping partners, email and analytics vendors, and
      professional advisers. We may disclose information if required by law, to protect rights and safety,
      or in connection with a merger, acquisition, or sale of assets. We do not sell personal information
      as a standalone product. If you are in a jurisdiction with a “sale” or “sharing” definition for
      advertising cookies, have counsel map those flows before launch.
    </p>
    <h2>7. Cookies and similar technologies</h2>
    <p>
      Shopify and optional apps may set cookies, pixels, and local storage for checkout, sessions, preferences,
      analytics, and advertising. You can control cookies through your browser. Blocking some cookies may
      affect cart and checkout. Configure a cookie banner and Shopify customer privacy settings to match
      the markets you serve.
    </p>
    <h2>8. Retention</h2>
    <p>
      We retain personal information for as long as needed for the purposes above, including order records
      required for tax and consumer law, then delete or anonymise it according to Shopify tools and our
      internal schedule. Retention periods must be confirmed by counsel and operations.
    </p>
    <h2>9. Security</h2>
    <p>
      We use Shopify’s platform controls and organisational measures appropriate to a small luxury house.
      No method of transmission or storage is perfectly secure. Please use a unique password for your
      customer account and contact us promptly if you suspect unauthorised access.
    </p>
    <h2>10. International transfers</h2>
    <p>
      Shopify and our providers may process data in countries other than your own, including Canada, the
      United States, and other locations where Shopify operates. Transfer safeguards (for example standard
      contractual clauses) should be confirmed against Shopify’s current data processing terms.
    </p>
    <h2>11. Your rights</h2>
    <p>
      Depending on your location, you may have rights to access, correct, delete, restrict, or port your
      data, to object to certain processing, and to withdraw consent. Customer account tools and Shopify
      privacy settings may help you exercise some of these rights. You may also contact us using the
      details above, and you may complain to a supervisory authority. Do not treat this list as exhaustive
      or as creating rights that local law does not grant.
    </p>
    <h2>12. Children</h2>
    <p>
      Maison Tavo is not directed to children. We do not knowingly collect personal information from
      children under the age required by applicable law. If you believe we have, contact us so we can delete it.
    </p>
    <h2>13. Changes</h2>
    <p>
      We may update this policy. The “last reviewed” date in the accompanying markdown source
      (<code>theme/legal/privacy.md</code>) should be updated when counsel signs off. Material changes may
      be announced on the storefront or by email where required.
    </p>
    <h2>14. Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Maison Tavo / Kartavya — privacy enquiries via
      {% if shop.email != blank %}{{ shop.email }}{% else %}the store contact form{% endif %}.
      Native Shopify policy, if published:
      {% if shop.privacy_policy %}
        <a href="{{ shop.privacy_policy.url }}">{{ shop.privacy_policy.title }}</a>.
      {% else %}
        not yet published in Admin → Settings → Policies.
      {% endif %}
    </p>

  {%- when 'terms' -%}
    <h2>1. Agreement</h2>
    <p>
      These Terms of Service are <strong>template copy requiring lawyer review</strong> and are not legal advice.
      They govern access to {{ shop.name }} and purchases of Maison Tavo products. The store is operated by
      Kartavya as a placeholder operator for this template. By using the site or placing an order you agree
      to these terms and to our Privacy Policy. If you do not agree, do not use the store.
    </p>
    <h2>2. Eligibility</h2>
    <p>
      You must be able to form a binding contract in your jurisdiction and must provide accurate checkout
      information. You are responsible for activity under your customer account.
    </p>
    <h2>3. Products and descriptions</h2>
    <p>
      We describe materials, colour, and fit with care, but photography, screens, and handmade variation mean
      that pieces may differ slightly from images. Editions may be limited. We may correct errors in pricing
      or description and refuse or cancel orders where we reasonably believe there is a mistake, fraud, or
      stock issue.
    </p>
    <h2>4. Orders, pricing, and payment</h2>
    <p>
      An order is an offer to buy. Acceptance occurs when we confirm the order or dispatch the goods, as
      specified at checkout. Prices are shown in the store currency and may exclude or include taxes and
      duties according to Shopify Markets configuration. Payment is processed by Shopify and the payment
      methods enabled on the store. You represent that you are authorised to use the selected method.
    </p>
    <h2>5. Shipping and risk</h2>
    <p>
      Delivery estimates are not guarantees. Risk and title pass according to the shipping terms stated at
      checkout and any Shipping Policy published in Shopify Admin. You are responsible for providing a
      deliverable address and for customs charges where applicable.
    </p>
    <h2>6. Returns, refunds, and cancellations</h2>
    <p>
      Returns follow the Refund Policy hosted by Shopify, if published, and any additional house rules
      stated on the product or cart. Unworn, unaltered pieces in original condition may be returnable within
      the stated window; made-to-order, final-sale, and intimate items may be excluded as disclosed before
      purchase. This paragraph must be aligned with consumer mandatory rights in each market of sale.
    </p>
    <h2>7. Intellectual property</h2>
    <p>
      The Maison Tavo name, marks, product designs, photography, copy, and storefront look are protected.
      See the Intellectual Property page (template <code>page.ipr</code>). You may not copy, scrape, or
      commercially reuse house content without written permission, except for brief fair quotation permitted by law.
    </p>
    <h2>8. Acceptable use</h2>
    <p>
      You may not misuse the store, attempt unauthorised access, interfere with checkout, submit unlawful
      content, or use the site to infringe others’ rights. We may suspend access where we reasonably suspect
      abuse.
    </p>
    <h2>9. Third-party services</h2>
    <p>
      Checkout, payments, reviews, and apps may be provided by third parties under their own terms.
      Shopify’s terms apply to platform features we do not control.
    </p>
    <h2>10. Disclaimer and limitation of liability</h2>
    <p>
      To the fullest extent permitted by law, the store and products are provided as described, and we
      exclude implied warranties that can legally be excluded. We are not liable for indirect, incidental,
      special, or consequential loss, or loss of profit, data, or goodwill, arising from use of the store
      or delay in delivery, except where liability cannot be limited (including death or personal injury
      caused by negligence, fraud, or mandatory consumer guarantees). Where liability can be limited, our
      aggregate liability relating to an order is limited to the amount you paid for that order.
    </p>
    <h2>11. Indemnity</h2>
    <p>
      You will indemnify Maison Tavo and Kartavya against claims arising from your misuse of the store or
      breach of these terms, to the extent permitted by law.
    </p>
    <h2>12. Governing law</h2>
    <p>
      These terms are governed by the laws of the jurisdiction in which the operator is established, without
      prejudice to mandatory consumer protections of your country of residence. Counsel must insert the
      actual governing law, venue, and any alternative dispute process before this store trades.
    </p>
    <h2>13. Changes</h2>
    <p>
      We may revise these terms by posting an updated version. Continued use after the effective date
      constitutes acceptance where permitted. For material changes affecting existing orders, the terms
      in force at purchase typically apply.
    </p>
    <h2>14. Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Maison Tavo / Kartavya —
      {% if shop.email != blank %}{{ shop.email }}{% else %}store contact form{% endif %}.
      Native Shopify terms, if published:
      {% if shop.terms_of_service %}
        <a href="{{ shop.terms_of_service.url }}">{{ shop.terms_of_service.title }}</a>.
      {% else %}
        not yet published in Admin → Settings → Policies.
      {% endif %}
    </p>

  {%- when 'ipr' -%}
    <h2>1. Purpose</h2>
    <p>
      This Intellectual Property notice is <strong>template copy requiring lawyer review</strong> and is not
      legal advice. It explains how Maison Tavo and Kartavya (placeholder operator) protect the house’s
      names, designs, imagery, and storefront, and how visitors may use them.
    </p>
    <h2>2. Ownership</h2>
    <p>
      Unless otherwise stated, all intellectual property in the Maison Tavo house, including trade marks,
      trade dress, product silhouettes, patterns, lookbook photography, film, copy, graphics, and the
      selection and arrangement of the storefront, is owned by Maison Tavo, Kartavya, or licensors.
      Purchase of a garment transfers the physical item, not the underlying design copyright, pattern,
      or brand rights, except as required by exhaustion or other mandatory law.
    </p>
    <h2>3. Trade marks</h2>
    <p>
      “Maison Tavo”, associated logos, and campaign names are trade marks or trade names, whether or not
      registered. You may not use them in a way that suggests endorsement, affiliation, or that you operate
      the house. Domain names, social handles, and metadata that imitate the house are not permitted.
    </p>
    <h2>4. Copyright</h2>
    <p>
      Site text, product stories, journal articles, and original photography are protected by copyright.
      You may view them for personal, non-commercial shopping. You may not reproduce galleries, scrape
      product data for competing catalogues, train models on house imagery where prohibited, or republish
      lookbooks without written consent.
    </p>
    <h2>5. Design and product rights</h2>
    <p>
      Maison Tavo products may be protected by design registrations, unregistered design rights, copyright
      in artistic craftsmanship, and trade dress. Copying, adapting, or manufacturing confusingly similar
      garments, hardware, or packaging for commercial purposes is prohibited.
    </p>
    <h2>6. Limited licence to visitors</h2>
    <p>
      We grant a limited, revocable, non-transferable licence to access the storefront and to download a
      copy of a page for personal reference. Framing, mirroring, or systematic extraction of the catalogue
      is outside this licence.
    </p>
    <h2>7. User submissions</h2>
    <p>
      If you send comments, photos, or reviews, you grant Maison Tavo a worldwide, royalty-free licence to
      use that content to operate and promote the house, while you retain ownership of your original
      copyright. Do not submit material you do not have rights to. We may remove content that infringes
      or violates these terms.
    </p>
    <h2>8. Third-party rights</h2>
    <p>
      Some fonts, stock, or platform components are licensed from third parties (including Shopify). Those
      licences do not grant you extra rights. Product names of other houses that appear in editorial
      comparison remain their owners’ property.
    </p>
    <h2>9. Notice of infringement</h2>
    <p>
      If you believe storefront content infringes your IP, send a notice with: (a) your contact details;
      (b) identification of the work; (c) the URL of the allegedly infringing material; (d) a statement
      of good-faith belief; and (e) a statement that the information is accurate and that you are the
      owner or authorised agent. We will consider valid notices and may remove or disable access. Counsel
      should add a jurisdiction-specific takedown process (for example DMCA) before targeting those markets.
    </p>
    <h2>10. Enforcement</h2>
    <p>
      We may investigate misuse, send cease-and-desist correspondence, use platform reporting tools, and
      seek injunctions or damages. Nothing in this notice limits remedies available at law.
    </p>
    <h2>11. Contact</h2>
    <p>
      IP enquiries: Maison Tavo / Kartavya —
      {% if shop.email != blank %}{{ shop.email }}{% else %}store contact form{% endif %}
      — and <a href="https://kartavya.tech" target="_blank" rel="noopener">kartavya.tech</a>.
      Source documentation for this page lives in <code>theme/legal/ipr.md</code>.
    </p>
{%- endcase -%}
